# locals: (state:)

# The submitter-facing answer to "how far along is this": a six-step
# vocabulary derived from the ingest status AND the curation rows, so the
# client never has to interpret either enum itself. Neither
# `SubmissionRequest.status` nor the nine Lifecycleable states are a
# progress scale on their own. See CurationState::STEPS.
#
# Shared by the list and the detail so a row and the page it opens can
# never disagree about where a request is.
{
  step:              CurationState::STEP_KEYS[state.current_step_index].to_s,
  failed:            state.failed?,
  closed:            state.closed?,
  row_count:         state.row_count,
  accessioned_count: state.accessioned_count,
  hold_date:         state.hold_date&.iso8601
}
